{"id":"n-20261025-bi0tt1","category":"gaming","display_title":"James Gunn Defends DCU Strategy","display_title_he":"ג'יימס גאן מגן על אסטרטגיית היקום הקולנועי","short_summary":"DC Studios co-chairman James Gunn recently explained his vision for the DCU, emphasizing that individual films should tell meaningful standalone stories rather than serving merely as setup for future crossovers.","english_level":"C1","words":493,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"IGN","domain":"ign.com","url":"https://www.ign.com/articles/james-gunn-defends-the-dcus-approach-to-interconnected-stories-doesnt-want-movies-like-clayface-to-exist-just-to-set-up-crossovers","title":"James Gunn Defends the DCU's Approach to Interconnected Stories, Doesn't Want Movies Like Clayface to Exist Just to 'Set Up' Crossovers","published_at":"2026-10-24T22:09:42.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-24T22:09:42.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-25T06:13:24.910Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The modern cinematic landscape is heavily dominated by sprawling franchises and interconnected universes, yet DC Studios co-chairman James Gunn recently stepped forward to defend a more deliberate approach to storytelling. According to statements shared on social media, Gunn firmly believes that individual films within the DCU should hold intrinsic value on their own, rather than existing solely to set up massive crossover events.","This philosophical stance became a prominent topic of discussion following the theatrical release of Clayface. The R-rated, bloody body horror feature explores the tragic story of Matt Hagen, portrayed by Tom Rhys Harries. Released appropriately in October, the movie molded its way into the comic book universe with an adult-oriented narrative. While the film has earned solid reviews from both critics and fans—including a 7/10 score from IGN—a faction of vocal watchers has continued to complain that studio executives Gunn and co-chairman Peter Safran are failing to build rapidly toward overarching tie-in projects. These critics argue that smaller entries should function primarily as stepping stones toward greater team-up spectacles, noting that projects like The People v. Gorilla Grodd appear further along while broader crossover moments remain limited.","Gunn, however, completely rejects this perspective. Replying to a supportive fan on the Threads platform, the co-chairman explained that the DCU functions as an expansive alternate universe where creators can enter at any location or time to tell a specific story. He expressed a strong dislike for the notion that individual narratives lack meaning unless they directly feed into something larger. Furthermore, Gunn pointed out that the Star Wars franchise has successfully utilized a similar approach for decades, though he acknowledged that the sci-fi giant lacks the sweeping tonal variety found in the DCU, which constantly shifts between serious drama, action, comedy, and horror.","Despite prioritizing standalone quality, Gunn assured audiences that connective tissue still binds the universe together. He noted that while major arcs like the Superman saga progress naturally across multiple releases—travelling from Superman into Man of Tomorrow and onward—those supporting projects are crafted to be enjoyed independently. People should watch Clayface because it functions as a compelling horror film in its own right, introducing a new Gotham City, not merely because of where the character might appear three movies down the line. Gunn and his colleagues are seemingly more interested in laying a worthy foundation than rushing into a massive team-up movie akin to the Justice League.","Alongside discussing overarching strategy, Gunn provided brief updates regarding other upcoming productions in the pipeline. Creature Commandos Season 2 is slated to arrive following the premiere of Man of Tomorrow next year. Speaking of the Superman sequel, Gunn revealed that a select group of individuals has recently viewed early director's cuts, a refining process he describes as exciting as he continuously recuts and screens versions for new eyes every Friday. Meanwhile, the Elseworlds sequel, The Batman Part 2, remains officially on track for its scheduled release on February 18, 2028, despite ongoing behind-the-scenes adjustments."],"facts":[{"fact":"DC Studios co-chairman James Gunn defended the DCU's interconnected storytelling approach on Threads.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Gunn stated he does not want movies like Clayface to exist purely to set up future crossovers.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Clayface is a bloody, R-rated body horror movie featuring the tragic story of Matt Hagen, played by Tom Rhys Harries.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Some DC watchers have complained that executives like Gunn and Peter Safran are not using smaller stories to build toward massive tie-in projects quickly enough.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The DCU officially launched with the animated series Creature Commandos before hitting theaters with Superman, followed by projects like Peacemaker Season 2, Supergirl, Lanterns, and Clayface.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Gunn compared the DCU's flexible universe structure to the long-standing approach of Star Wars.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Gunn noted that the DCU features significant tonal variety, moving between serious drama, action, comedy, and horror.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"A small group of people has recently viewed director's cuts of the upcoming Superman sequel, Man of Tomorrow.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Elseworlds sequel, The Batman Part 2, is currently scheduled for release on February 18, 2028.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"modern","lemma":"modern","pos":"adjective","he":"מודרני","name":false},{"text":"cinematic","lemma":"cinematic","pos":"adjective","he":"קולנועי","name":false},{"text":"landscape","lemma":"landscape","pos":"noun","he":"נוף","name":false}